CRUD Operations in Neo4j - Social Network Database

1. Create a social network database with nodes: User (UserID, Username) and relationships: (FOLLOWS)
Cypher

CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u1', Username: 'Alice'});
CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u2', Username: 'Bob'});
CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u3', Username: 'Charlie'});
CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u4', Username: 'Jane'});
CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u5', Username: 'David'});
CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u6', Username: 'Eve'});

MATCH (a:User {Username: 'Alice'}), (b:User {Username: 'Bob'}) CREATE (a)-[:FOLLOWS]->(b);
MATCH (a:User {Username: 'Alice'}), (c:User {Username: 'Charlie'}) CREATE (a)-[:FOLLOWS]->(c);
MATCH (b:User {Username: 'Bob'}), (d:User {Username: 'Jane'}) CREATE (b)-[:FOLLOWS]->(d);
MATCH (c:User {Username: 'Charlie'}), (d:User {Username: 'Jane'}) CREATE (c)-[:FOLLOWS]->(d);
MATCH (d:User {Username: 'Jane'}), (a:User {Username: 'Alice'}) CREATE (d)-[:FOLLOWS]->(a);
MATCH (d:User {Username: 'Jane'}), (e:User {Username: 'David'}) CREATE (d)-[:FOLLOWS]->(e);
MATCH (e:User {Username: 'David'}), (f:User {Username: 'Eve'}) CREATE (e)-[:FOLLOWS]->(f);
MATCH (f:User {Username: 'Eve'}), (a:User {Username: 'Alice'}) CREATE (f)-[:FOLLOWS]->(a);
MATCH (a:User {Username: 'Alice'}), (d:User {Username: 'Jane'}) CREATE (a)-[:FOLLOWS]->(d);

2. Write a query to display all users.
Cypher

MATCH (u:User) RETURN u.Username, u.UserID;

3. Write a query to display users followed by a specific user with Username "Jane".
Cypher

MATCH (u:User {Username: 'Jane'})-[:FOLLOWS]->(followedUser:User) RETURN followedUser.Username;

4. Write a query to display all users in ascending order by Username.
Cypher

MATCH (u:User) RETURN u.Username ORDER BY u.Username ASC;

5. Write a query to find all users who follow both "Alice" and "Bob".
Cypher

MATCH (follower:User)-[:FOLLOWS]->(alice:User {Username: 'Alice'}),
      (follower)-[:FOLLOWS]->(bob:User {Username: 'Bob'})
RETURN DISTINCT follower.Username;

6. Write a query to find users with the most number of followers.
Cypher

MATCH (follower:User)-[:FOLLOWS]->(followedUser:User)
RETURN followedUser.Username, COUNT(follower) AS NumberOfFollowers
ORDER BY NumberOfFollowers DESC
LIMIT 1;

7. Display first 5 users:
Cypher

MATCH (u:User) RETURN u.Username LIMIT 5;














CRUD Operations in Neo4j - Movie Recommendation Database

1. Create a Movie Recommendation Database with nodes: Movie (MovieID, Title) and User (UserID, Username), and relationships: (LIKES) indicating a user likes a specific movie.
Cypher

CREATE (:Movie {MovieID: 'm1', Title: 'Inception'});
CREATE (:Movie {MovieID: 'm2', Title: 'The Matrix'});
CREATE (:Movie {MovieID: 'm3', Title: 'Interstellar'});
CREATE (:Movie {MovieID: 'm4', Title: 'Pulp Fiction'});
CREATE (:Movie {MovieID: 'm5', Title: 'Avatar'});

CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u101', Username: 'John'});
CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u102', Username: 'Sara'});
CREATE (:User {UserID: 'u103', Username: 'Mike'});

MATCH (j:User {Username: 'John'}), (i:Movie {Title: 'Inception'}) CREATE (j)-[:LIKES]->(i);
MATCH (j:User {Username: 'John'}), (m:Movie {Title: 'The Matrix'}) CREATE (j)-[:LIKES]->(m);
MATCH (s:User {Username: 'Sara'}), (i:Movie {Title: 'Inception'}) CREATE (s)-[:LIKES]->(i);
MATCH (s:User {Username: 'Sara'}), (t:Movie {Title: 'Interstellar'}) CREATE (s)-[:LIKES]->(t);
MATCH (k:User {Username: 'Mike'}), (m:Movie {Title: 'The Matrix'}) CREATE (k)-[:LIKES]->(m);
MATCH (k:User {Username: 'Mike'}), (p:Movie {Title: 'Pulp Fiction'}) CREATE (k)-[:LIKES]->(p);

2. Write a query to display all movies liked by a specific user with Username "John".
Cypher

MATCH (u:User {Username: 'John'})-[:LIKES]->(m:Movie) RETURN m.Title;

3. Write a query to find all users who like the movie titled "Inception".
Cypher

MATCH (u:User)-[:LIKES]->(m:Movie {Title: 'Inception'}) RETURN u.Username;

4. Write a query to display all movies in ascending order by Title.
Cypher

MATCH (m:Movie) RETURN m.Title ORDER BY m.Title ASC;

5. Write a query to find all users who like both "The Matrix" and "Inception".
Cypher

MATCH (u:User)-[:LIKES]->(m1:Movie {Title: 'The Matrix'}),
      (u)-[:LIKES]->(m2:Movie {Title: 'Inception'})
RETURN DISTINCT u.Username;

6. Write a query to find the most liked movie.
Cypher

MATCH (u:User)-[:LIKES]->(m:Movie)
RETURN m.Title, COUNT(u) AS NumberOfLikes
ORDER BY NumberOfLikes DESC
LIMIT 1;

7. Write a query to display the top 5 users who like the most movies.
Cypher

MATCH (u:User)-[:LIKES]->(m:Movie)
RETURN u.Username, COUNT(m) AS NumberOfMoviesLiked
ORDER BY NumberOfMoviesLiked DESC
LIMIT 5;
